<h1>Setup</h1>
<p class="subtitle">One-time setup for a fresh fork of this dashboard. Fill this in once, right after forking — it configures this repo's site settings and adds your first class, straight from the browser.</p>

<form id="form-setup" class="manage-form">
  <section>
    <h2>Your repo</h2>
    <label>Repo (<code>owner/repo</code>)<input type="text" name="repo" placeholder="yourname/academic-tracker" required></label>
    <p class="hint">The GitHub repo this fork lives in — everything below commits directly to it via the GitHub API.</p>

    <h2>GitHub token</h2>
    <p>Create a <strong>fine-grained personal access token</strong> at
      <a href="https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new">github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new</a>,
      scoped to just the repo you typed above, with these repository permissions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contents:</strong> Read and write</li>
      <li><strong>Actions:</strong> Read and write <span class="hint">— lets it trigger a rebuild right after a commit</span></li>
      <li><strong>Metadata:</strong> Read-only <span class="hint">— required by GitHub for every fine-grained token</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="hint">The token is stored only in this browser's local storage — never written to any file in the repo. Once saved here, <a href="{{ '/settings/' | url }}">Settings</a> and <a href="{{ '/manage/' | url }}">Manage</a> already have it too.</p>
    <label>Token<input type="password" name="token" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="github_pat_…" required></label>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Site</h2>
    <label>Title<input type="text" name="title" placeholder="My Academic Dashboard" required></label>
    <label>Current term<input type="text" name="current_term" placeholder="Fall 2026" required></label>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>First class <span class="hint">(optional — skip and add classes from <a href="{{ '/manage/' | url }}">Manage</a> later if you'd rather)</span></h2>
    <label>Code<input type="text" name="code" placeholder="CS 420"></label>
    <label>ID (slug — optional, derived from the code if left blank)<input type="text" name="id" placeholder="cs420"></label>
    <label>Name<input type="text" name="name" placeholder="Full course title"></label>
    <label>Term<input type="text" name="term" placeholder="e.g. same as Current Term above"></label>
    <label>Instructor<input type="text" name="instructor"></label>
    <label>Meeting times<input type="text" name="meeting_times" placeholder="Tue/Thu 2:35–3:50pm, Room 213"></label>
    <label>Color<input type="color" name="color" value="#2b6cb0"></label>
    <label>Course site link (optional)<input type="url" name="materials_link"></label>
  </section>

  <label class="setup-confirm">
    <input type="checkbox" name="confirm" required>
    This will set this repo's site title/term and add this class — only needed once, right after forking. Running it again on an already-configured repo will overwrite its title and term.
  </label>

  <button type="submit">Set up my instance</button>
  <p class="form-status"></p>
</form>

<script type="module" src="{{ '/js/setup.js' | url }}"></script>
